Liquid Personnel is recruiting a &nbsp;Children’s Social Worker to join its client’s Family Court Advise team, based in Peterborough.

What will your responsibilities be? &nbsp;

• Conduct safeguarding checks and risk assessments within family court proceedings.

• Gather, analyse, and evaluate complex information relating to child welfare and protection concerns.

• Prepare high-quality court reports, statements, and recommendations.

• Represent and advocate for the child's wishes, feelings, and best interests.

• Undertake direct work with children, young people, and families.

• Provide expert advice to courts on safeguarding and welfare matters.

• Manage a varied caseload across Public Law and Private Law proceedings.

• Work effectively with local authorities, legal representatives, schools, healthcare professionals, and partner agencies.

• Support the delivery of the&nbsp;Child Focused Court Model (CFC), ensuring children's voices remain central throughout proceedings.

• Maintain accurate case records and utilise case management systems effectively.&nbsp;

Qualifications and Experience: &nbsp;

To be successful in this role you must have; &nbsp;

• Social Work England registration &nbsp;

• Eligible to work in the UK &nbsp;

• Hold a full UK driving licence &nbsp;

• Post-qualified experience &nbsp;

• Degree level or equivalent in Social Work &nbsp;

Why Liquid Personnel? &nbsp;

• Free DBS and compliance service

• Twice weekly payroll and ‘Faster Pay’ service, getting you paid more quickly

• Access to exclusive roles that aren’t available from other agencies &nbsp;

• Free access to Liquid’s exclusive social work training and CPD portal &nbsp;

• Your own dedicated consultant with extensive social work knowledge &nbsp;

